      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T17:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I understand it (might have it wrong!), this `bta_av_api_register` is called through `BTA_AvRegister` once for Source and once for Sink.\n\nThe Source side, as configured on most phones, ends up skipping chunks of this function because avrcp_service is a thing.\n\nThe Sink side executes this function to the end.\n\nWith that understanding, how does this make a true source and sink configuration and thus true merged SDP record? Is it relying on `btif_av_src_sink_coexist_enabled()`? If so, we want to do away with this sysprop.\n\nI would instead use the profile supported sysprops, or change the pattern such that each profile subjects it\u0027s desired set of features, etc. on the config, and thus SDP record, when they start.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 483,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 486,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "97b6de4e2f90081df183a48ae6ed76c08f98b757",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
